<title>USA: Raytheon debt to climb to $6.6 billion.</title>
<headline>Raytheon debt to climb to $6.6 billion.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co said Monday its debt would total $6.6 billion following its acquisition of Texas Instruments Inc's defense business.</p>
<p>Raytheon's debt-to-capital ratio after the $2.95 billion deal will be about 59 percent, Robert McWade, a Raytheon spokesman, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We have a plan in place to bring that debt down. We know we can do it,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Despite the debt, Raytheon will &quot;retain significant flexibility to operate our business and to take other actions we might deem necessary because we can operate from a position of strength,&quot; McWade said.</p>
<p>((-- Boston Bureau (617) 367-4176))</p>
